00:10:14,338 --> 00:10:16,671
before any other store,

294
00:10:16,671 --> 00:10:20,213
and every visit feeds the advertising

295
00:10:20,213 --> 00:10:21,404
machine.

296
00:10:21,650 --> 00:10:24,540
Let me put the whole machine together.

297
00:10:24,620 --> 00:10:27,180
A fee that locks in the habit.

298
00:10:27,180 --> 00:10:29,327
Shipping and video that make the fee

299
00:10:29,327 --> 00:10:31,120
feel like a bargain.

300
00:10:31,350 --> 00:10:33,483
Advertising that profits from all that

301
00:10:33,483 --> 00:10:34,510
traffic.

302
00:10:34,680 --> 00:10:37,490
A cloud business that throws off cash.

303
00:10:37,540 --> 00:10:39,018
And an exit door that was,

304
00:10:39,018 --> 00:10:40,684
according to regulators,

305
00:10:40,684 --> 00:10:42,968
deliberately hard to find.

306
00:10:43,217 --> 00:10:46,055
So what is the hidden economics of

307
00:10:46,055 --> 00:10:47,687
Amazon Prime?

308
00:10:48,137 --> 00:10:49,710
Prime is not a product that has

309
00:10:49,710 --> 00:10:51,687
to make money on its own.

310
00:10:51,917 --> 00:10:53,597
It is the glue.

311
00:10:53,617 --> 00:10:56,095
It keeps hundreds of millions of people

312
00:10:56,095 --> 00:10:56,814
shopping,

313
00:10:56,814 --> 00:10:59,397
watching and clicking in one place.

314
00:10:59,777 --> 00:11:02,260
Amazon may spend more on delivery than

315
00:11:02,260 --> 00:11:03,687
Prime fees bring in.

316
00:11:03,837 --> 00:11:05,639
But what it buys with that money

317
00:11:05,639 --> 00:11:08,267
is something far more valuable.

318
00:11:08,417 --> 00:11:10,009
Your habit.

319
00:11:10,250 --> 00:11:12,170
Next time on The Hidden Economics,

320
00:11:12,170 --> 00:11:14,461
we follow the money behind another hidden

321
00:11:14,461 --> 00:11:16,420
link of the world economy.

322
00:11:16,420 --> 00:11:18,547
This is The Hidden Economics.
